🚀 Level-3: Substring / Subsequence Patterns
        Pattern 7️⃣ All Substrings Pattern (Brute Force)
        👉 Generate every substring for analysis.
            Common Problems:
            1. Count palindromic substrings
            2. Find substring with specific sum or pattern
        Pattern 8️⃣ Subsequence Pattern (Recursive / Bitmask)
        👉 Used for combinations and string subsets.
           Examples:
           1. Generate all subsequences
           2. Find the longest common subsequence


🏆 Summary of All String Patterns
| Level | Pattern        | Use                         |
| ----- | -------------- | --------------------------- |
| 1     | Traversal      | Basic character operations  |
| 1     | Reverse        | String manipulation         |
| 1     | Palindrome     | Checks, two-pointer intro   |
| 1     | Frequency      | HashMap skills              |
| 2     | Two-Pointer    | Efficient scanning          |
| 2     | Sliding Window | Optimal substring problems  |
| 3     | Substring      | Pattern search, brute force |
| 3     | Subsequence    | Recursive patterns          |
| 4     | StringBuilder  | Efficient editing           |
| 4     | Splitting      | Word-level operations       |
| 4     | Sorting        | Anagram problems            |
| 5     | HashMap        | Complex patterns            |
| 5     | Regex          | Validation                  |
| 5     | DP             | Hard interview problems     |
